  "notes": "Trackmasters replay rather than chop, and that single production fact is what every parameter here follows from. Because the source is re-performed on keyboards and strings rather than lifted, the harmony has real functional motion — I–V–vi–IV on the interpolated singles and ii–V–I underneath — and the bass is a played instrument, so it is `independent_riff` with `followRootsProb` 0.55 and P8 in `passingTones` for the octave jumps the research names. The clap-layered backbeat and the 16th hat runs into the hooks are the other two distinctives; `hihat.fillDensity` is 0.58 so the runs are audible without the base pattern leaving 8ths. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates this entry medium-high: the replay method is documented first-hand by the producers, but the tempo band and the drum velocities are catalog-level, and the exact split between major singles and minor street cuts is carried as scale weights rather than as two authored modes.",
